)","power":null,"produced_mana":["G"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land — Forest"}],"rulings":[{"oracle_id":"db5a4c25-5ae5-4a04-be79-bdee39b9152c","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc","comment":"If a player controls no creatures, or each creature they control is a Zombie, that player does nothing when the first ability resolves."},{"oracle_id":"db5a4c25-5ae5-4a04-be79-bdee39b9152c","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc","comment":"In a Two-Headed Giant game, Call to the Grave will trigger twice during each team's upkeep, once for each player. Each of the two players will sacrifice a non-Zombie creature when the ability referring to that player resolves."},{"oracle_id":"db5a4c25-5ae5-4a04-be79-bdee39b9152c","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc","comment":"If there is at least one creature on the battlefield at the beginning of the end step, the last ability won't trigger. If it does trigger, but a creature enters before it resolves, the ability won't do anything when it resolves. Call to the Grave's controller won't sacrifice it."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc","comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\"."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands."},{"oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc","comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks."}]}
